          <!-- BODY -->
          <tr>
            <td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">

              <p>Hello fellow hams,</p>

              <p>
                The season finale is here: a full-scale
                <strong>regional mobile T-hunt</strong> across
                west Snohomish County, finishing with a short
                on-foot leg at a location disclosed to
                registered participants.
              </p>

              <p>
                This is a different kind of hunt from July and
                August. Instead of walking a park on foot, you
                will be <strong>driving</strong> across the
                hunt area, taking bearings from multiple locations
                to triangulate the fox&rsquo;s location. Once
                you are close, you park and complete the final
                leg on foot to the fox.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Event Details
              </h3>
              <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                     border="0"
                     style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;">
                <tr>
                  <td width="140"
                      style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Date:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Sunday, September 20, 2026</strong>
                    (tentative)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Hunt start:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Morning &mdash; exact start time and
                    starting location TBD; watch for an
                    update closer to the event
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                  Hunt area:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                  <strong>West Snohomish County:</strong> south of
                  Marysville, west of SR-9, north of the
                  Snohomish/King county line, east of Puget Sound
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Frequency:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex</strong>
                    (callsign K7LED); net control on K7LED repeater
                    (alt 146.580&nbsp;MHz FM simplex)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Fox power:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Byonics MicroFox (single fox); verify coverage
                    from launch point during site walk
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Hunt type:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Mobile T-hunt (drive to bearings) with
                    short on-foot final leg
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What to Bring
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Vehicle</strong> and a co-pilot if
                  possible &mdash; one person drives, one
                  takes bearings
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Mobile or handheld radio on
                  147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Directional antenna &mdash; a Yagi on the
                  vehicle roof mount or a handheld tape-measure
                  Yagi for bearing checks
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Step attenuator for close-in hunting during
                  the final on-foot leg
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Washington state road map or mapping
                  application for triangulating bearings
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Comfortable walking shoes for the final
                  on-foot leg
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Water, snacks, and a full tank of fuel
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                About this hunt area
              </h3>
              <p>
                The September mobile course is confined to west
                Snohomish County and is designed for drive-in
                bearing work across urban-edge and suburban RF
                terrain. The final on-foot leg and social wrap-up
                location will be disclosed to registered
                participants on hunt day.
              </p>

              <p style="background-color:#fce4e4;border-left:4px solid
                        #c62828;padding:12px 16px;margin:20px 0;
                        font-size:14px;">
                <strong>Safety note:</strong> Stay on public roads
                and legal pedestrian routes only, and follow all
                site-specific instructions provided at launch.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                RSVP &amp; Questions
              </h3>
              <p>
                A head count helps us plan the event logistics.
                Reply to this message or contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                [TOM-EMAIL].
              </p>

              <p>
                More details &mdash; including the exact launch
                point and finish location &mdash; will come in the
                reminder email closer to the event. Watch your inbox!
              </p>

              <p>
                We look forward to seeing you for the season
                finale. 73 de KE4HET
              </p>

